title start
kind: decision
tags: decision
Decision page: record one choice and why
title end

paragraph start
Use a decision page when you choose between options and want the reason to survive. Fill each section below and replace this text with your own.
paragraph end

section start
title start
Context
title end

paragraph start
Say what forces the choice now: the problem, the limits, and what happens if nothing changes. Write it so a stranger understands it a year from now. Keep it short and factual.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Options
title end

paragraph start
List the realistic ways to solve it, one sentence each, and say which you rejected and why. A rejected option written down stops the same argument from coming back.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Decision
title end

paragraph start
State the one choice you made, in a sentence someone can act on. No hedging and no list of maybes.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Consequences
title end

paragraph start
Say what becomes easier, and above all what becomes harder, because of this choice. This is the part you will be glad to have in a year.
paragraph end

section end

comment start
one decision: context, options, decision, consequences
comment end

